## Institution deduplication rules

- Create an institution once, using a stable ID.
- Normalize names for duplicate detection while preserving the official display name.
- Match case and whitespace variations without accidentally merging different institutions.
- Do not automatically merge potentially different institutions just because their names resemble each other.
- Add a review mechanism for suspected duplicate records.
- Make the seed operation idempotent: running it again must not recreate the same institutions or duplicate FDRs.
- Do not delete existing data blindly. Identify duplicates, preserve valid references, and migrate or reconcile relationships safely.
- Enforce suitable uniqueness constraints or transactional checks where supported.
- Provide a controlled admin workflow for resolving duplicate institution records.

## Important distinction

**An institution appearing on several FDR rows is not automatically a duplicate.** One institution may legitimately have multiple FDRs.

The “My FDRs & Deposits” table should show one row per distinct FDR record. Repeated institution names across different FDRs are acceptable, but every row must link to the correct canonical institution.

Institution directories, institution dropdowns, and institution master lists should list each institution once. Use institution IDs for joins, filters, grouping, and navigation.

